# PublicPaymentWebhookApi — com.asrevo.cvhome.payment.api.v1.payment.PublicPaymentWebhookApi
#
# The provider telling payment what became of a checkout session. Public by necessity — Stripe holds no token of
# ours — so the store's own webhook secret is the credential: the store id is in the path, and the delivery is
# verified against that store's payment_configuration.webhook_secret. Addressed the way Stripe reaches it: through
# the pod edge (spg strips the /payment prefix), which is what lcl's stripe-org1-store1-webhook listener forwards to.
#
# A real delivery is easiest from the Stripe CLI: `stripe trigger checkout.session.completed` while the listener is
# up. The blocks below hand-sign a session-completed event with WEBHOOK_SECRET (the secret configured for the store;
# http-client.private.env.json). Today the endpoint answers 200 to every delivery and verifies the signature later,
# on the outbox — a bad signature is visible only as a transaction that stays PENDING. Phase 5 of
# .agents/plans/authorization-audit.md moves the check in front of the outbox and adds the 4xx blocks here.
#
# Requires a running stack: lcl start -d

### a signed checkout.session.completed — 200; the referenced transaction settles to PAID via the outbox
# The signature is Stripe's scheme, t=<epoch>,v1=<hmac-sha256 hex of "<epoch>.<payload>">, over the exact body
# bytes; compute it for the body below with WEBHOOK_SECRET and paste the whole header value into STRIPE_SIGNATURE
# (a pre-request script cannot read the body). GATEWAY_REF is set by external-payment-gateway-api.http's initiate.
POST {{SPG_URL}}/payment/api/v1/public/webhook/{{STORE_ID}}/STRIPE
Content-Type: application/json
Stripe-Signature: {{STRIPE_SIGNATURE}}

{"id":"evt_http_1","object":"event","api_version":"2024-06-20","type":"checkout.session.completed","data":{"object":{"id":"cs_http_1","object":"checkout.session","client_reference_id":"{{GATEWAY_REF}}"}}}

### no signature header — 200 today, and the transaction stays PENDING (WHK-01)
POST {{SPG_URL}}/payment/api/v1/public/webhook/{{STORE_ID}}/STRIPE
Content-Type: application/json

{"id":"evt_http_2","object":"event","api_version":"2024-06-20","type":"checkout.session.completed","data":{"object":{"id":"cs_http_2","object":"checkout.session","client_reference_id":"{{GATEWAY_REF}}"}}}

### a type the pod has no processor for — 200 today, discarded on the outbox
POST {{SPG_URL}}/payment/api/v1/public/webhook/{{STORE_ID}}/PAYPAL
Content-Type: application/json

{"event":"nothing-handles-this"}
